+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Customers can create, pay and cancel orders, and admins can manage coupons, but there is no way to attach a coupon to an order. This change lets a customer apply exactly one valid coupon to a pending order so the payable amount is reduced.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` accepting `{ "couponCode": string }`.
+- On success, update the order's `discountCents`, `finalAmountCents`, `couponCode`, insert a `coupon_redemptions` row and increment `coupons.used_count` atomically.
+- Normalize the coupon code (trim + uppercase) before lookup.
+- Enforce coupon validity window, active status, minimum amount, usage limit and discount capping.
+- Return the updated order with the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`; reject with the project's standard error envelope and specified codes.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `order-coupons`: applying a single coupon to a pending order, including validation, discount computation and atomic redemption bookkeeping.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+<!-- none -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- New route in `src/routes/orders.ts`, new business logic in `src/services/orderService.ts`, new SQL in `src/repositories/orderRepository.ts` and `src/repositories/couponRepository.ts`.
+- Requires a transaction spanning order update, redemption insert, and coupon counter update.
+- No schema changes, no new dependencies, no changes to existing routes' behavior.
+- New tests added under `tests/`.
