+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, now)` that updates the order, inserts a `coupon_redemptions` row and increments `coupons.used_count` inside one `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` transaction with `ROLLBACK` on error. Verify with a repository-level check that all three rows change together.
+
+## 2. Service logic
+
+- [x] 2.1 Change `OrderService` to receive the `CouponRepository` and update `createApp` wiring in `src/app.ts`. Verify `npm run build` succeeds.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with normalization, the section-6 error ordering, discount computation (FIXED/PERCENT, `Math.round`, cap, amount floor) using the injected `Clock`, then the atomic write and `return this.get(id)`. Verify all `order-coupons` scenarios in `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` pass.
+
+## 3. HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parsing `:id` and forwarding `body.couponCode`. Verify a successful route call returns 200 with the `GET /orders/:id` body.
+
+## 4. Tests
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add `tests/applyCoupon.test.ts` covering AC-01, AC-02, AC-04, AC-06, AC-07, AC-08, AC-09, AC-10, percent capping (AC-03), invalid bodies, unknown/inactive/expired coupons, usage exhaustion, minimum-not-met and error precedence. Verify `npm test` passes.
+
+## 5. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 5.1 Run `npm run build` and `npm test` and confirm both pass without modifying existing tests.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after implementation and verification complete.
